@startuml
autonumber
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 170

participant "Heartbeat\n(server-side)" as Heartbeat
participant "ClientConnection\n(SocketClientHandler /\nRmiClientHandler)" as Conn
participant "GameController" as Controller
participant "GameModel" as Model
participant "PlayerVirtualView\n(Observer, per client)" as Observer
participant "PersistenceManager" as Persistence
participant "Remaining Client\n(ConnectionManager + View)" as Client

== Disconnection handling (base requirement: terminate + notify) ==
note over Heartbeat, Conn
  A dropped client is detected by the heartbeat: a socket read timeout, or a failed
  RMI ping. Either way the server-side connection disconnects exactly once.
end note
Heartbeat -> Conn: disconnect()
activate Conn
Conn -> Controller: handleDisconnect()
activate Controller

note right of Controller: synchronized(model)
Controller -> Model: notifyDisconnection()
activate Model
Model -> Observer: onModelChanged(PLAYER_DISCONNECTED)
activate Observer
Observer -> Client: GameAbortedMessage
deactivate Observer
deactivate Model

Controller -> Persistence: deleteSave()
note right of Controller: the aborted game must not be resumed.

Controller -> Controller: terminate the aborted game
Controller --> Conn: return
deactivate Controller
deactivate Conn

== Client side ==
Client -> Client: handleUpdate(GameAbortedMessage)
note right of Client
  ConnectionManager's terminalDetector sets terminated = true,
  then relays the message.
end note
Client -> Client: accept -> visit(GameAbortedMessage): show "game aborted" screen

... the connection to the server is closed ...
Client -> Client: handleDisconnect()
note right of Client
  terminated == true -> reconnection is skipped: the drop is expected,
  there is nothing left to come back to.
end note

note over Heartbeat, Client
  Different from an UNEXPECTED server crash (no GameAbortedMessage): there
  terminated stays false, so the client keeps retrying and, once the server
  restarts and reloads its save, the player reconnects (FA Persistence).
end note
@enduml
